        "date": "2026-11-09T17:51:44Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): fixture library - save, insert and delete user fixtures\n\nA user fixture library (#339 slice 6): one `fixtures.camfixtures` file\nin the user fixtures folder (CAMCRAFT_FIXTURES, else\n<data dir>/camcraft/fixtures, beside #383's machines folder), in a\nversioned `camcraft-fixtures/1` JSON envelope shaped like the tool\nlibrary's. Each entry is a name, an optional note, the mesh in the\nfixture's own model frame, and the placement datum inside that frame.\n\n- app::fixture_library: a strict reader that refuses the whole file by\n  entry name, and a byte-stable writer. The store resolves the folder,\n  writes atomically, asks before replacing a name (Exists), and deletes\n  an entry.\n- commands::InsertFixture: one undo unit. It adds a model with the\n  entry's facets, places it at P ∘ D⁻¹ so the datum lands on the pick,\n  and tags it to the setup. A name already in the document takes\n  \"(2)\". The result is an ordinary tagged model, with no new project\n  key.\n- ui: the Fixtures node menu gains \"Save fixture to library…\" and\n  \"Insert from library…\". Both open modal dialogs: checked fixtures,\n  datum and note for a save; the entry list, datum origin and rotation,\n  Insert, and Delete with a confirmation for an insert.\n\nPinned by app fixture_library (6) and ui fixture_library_tests (4).\nThe slice-4 menu-label test now lists the two new rows.\n\nRefs #339\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
